00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.860 align:start position:0%
 
how mobility  affects my business so when I started  this business just over a decade ago I  felt like I needed to have an office and  a team and a place for everybody to come  work every day  fast forward a decade I've grown my team  that 15 people sold my office and  everybody works remotely from around the  world I get as much work done on this  and on this as I do my regular computer  so when Stephen Kelly the CEO of one of  my favorite companies sage tweeted me  asking me about how I use mobility in my  company I had to make a video response  not that long ago I did a thank-you  Thursday recognizing one of the social  media managers at Sage Gregg Tirico as  well so I thought I'd share with you the  five apps that I use every day on my  tablet to improve my productivity and  how you can too the first one is Gmail  now it's not surprising to have an email  app on your tablet but I used even a  little bit differently you see I have  two folders on Gmail one folders for all  my important contacts that's my team my  family my customers media Steven if you  were to write to me you would go to that  important contact folder and I checked  those every single day from my laptop in  the morning everybody else goes to a  general folder and they only answer them  from my tablet I answered them when I'm  shopping with my wife at a mall I  answered them when I'm standing in line  at the Department of Motor Vehicles I  answer them when I'm bored and yes I  answered them even in the bathroom I  find it's a huge productivity boost for  me that I get my important emails out  every morning from my computer and then  having that general inbox everybody else  answering from my tablet my second app  is Evernote I keep a lot of the  information about my business and a lot  of the day to day tasks in Evernote it's  a great way to keep notes remind  yourself the things that you have to do  and keep on top of the activities that  are happening in your business whenever  I'm on the go and I have an idea I'm  launching a new Evernote note and I'm  writing a damn whenever I'm meeting  somebody at a coffee shop or at their  office I'm bringing my tablet and I'm  opening up an Evernote file to take  notes in our meeting that note instantly  gets synced with not only my tablet but  also my laptop and my computer so I have  access to that information anywhere that  I go I also have shared notebooks with  people on my team as a to-do list so I  can see what they're doing what's coming  up next and how  progress is and the mobile version is  great when you're traveling I'll open up  a new notebook for every city that I'm  visiting and keep track of everything  that I have to do in that city people  are meeting destinations I want to go to  restaurants I want to check out all  available at your fingertips Evernote is  free is a basic package and I'm on the  premium version which is maybe five or  ten dollars a month  my number three app is feedly feedly is  a free app that lets you aggregate your  RSS feeds so if you're a subscriber to  any blogs or news websites you can get  all of their updates through your tablet  I used to use Google Reader and I loved  Google Reader but they canceled it  Google why did you cancel that you're  killing me but luckily feedly was here  to save the day so I'll use feedly to  stay on top of my favorite blogs and  news and usually it's when I'm bored and  usually before going to bed I'll usually  pop up my tablet and read up on all the  information I miss during the day my  number 4 app is Dropbox  Dropbox is a really cool way to be able  to sync files and folders across  multiple devices so kind of like  Evernote but instead of just sharing  text files you're sharing actual big  files so for example if I had a big  presentation downtown I could make a PDF  on my computer save it to Dropbox and  then just bring my tablet with me and  loaded here and will be automatically  synced just like every node I also share  Dropbox folders with people on my team  they could drop files in there I could  drop files in there  and anytime I want to pull them up  they're available on my tablet on my  laptop or on my desktop my number 5 app  is YouTube YouTube has quickly become my  favorite place to be on social media I  like it because one the content seems to  last longer a video will last a lot  longer than a tweet or Facebook post and  I just love the audience and the  community that are on YouTube my  favorite part of my day is waking up  every day and going to my laptop and  pulling up YouTube and responding and  seeing all the comments that come in but  it's starting to get out of control I  get so many comments and I love you guys  keep commenting away I love it so much  when I'm running out of time I know  probably at some point I'll have to give  up the comments because right now I'm  responding to everybody personally if  you see a comment coming  for me it's actually coming from me so I  find that having the YouTube app on my  tablet as well gives me extra time to  respond to your comment because I love  hearing from you guys now it's a bonus  app I'm going to throw fieldrunners in  there  fueled runners is a game that my wife  has become obsessed with I almost don't  get to see this thing anymore because  she's using us so much for field runners  so if you want to make your wife happy  download the field runners game and have  fun with it but you may not see your  tablet again so that's how my business  has gone mobile Steven thank you for the  great question and congrats on running  such a fantastic business for those who  watch and I'd love to know what of the  must-have apps that you use on a regular  basis leave your favorite apps in the  comments below and if you liked this  video continue to believe and subscribe  to the channel thank you guys so much  for watching I'll see you soon sign up  for the newsletter for more believe  you

